wift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlforpart\/transpose"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLForPart"]]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLForPart/transpose":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLForPart\/transpose","type":"topic","title":"transpose","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"transpose"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLTransposeV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTranspose"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLTransposeV7ContentV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Content"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The chromatic element in a part-transpose element will usually have a non-zero value, since octave"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transpositions can be represented in concert scores using the transpose element."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlforpart\/transpose"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTranspose/Content-swift.struct":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The transpose group represents what must be added to a written pitch to get a correct sounding pitch."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltranspose\/content-swift.struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Content","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLTranspose.Content","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Content","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTranspose\/Content-swift.struct","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLForPart":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLForPart","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLForPart","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The for-part type is used in a concert score to indicate the transposition for a transposed part created from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that score. It is only used in score files that contain a concert-score element in the defaults. This allows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"concert scores with transposed parts to be represented in a single uncompressed MusicXML file."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLForPart"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLForPart"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlforpart"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTranspose":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The transpose type represents what must be added to a written pitch to get a correct sounding pitch. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optional number attribute refers to staff numbers, from top to bottom on the system. If absent, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transposition applies to all staves in the part. Per-staff transposition is most often used in parts that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"represent multiple instruments."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltranspose","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTranspose","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLTranspose","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLTranspose","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTranspose","role":"symbol"}}}